    "https://careers.uwf.edu/jobs/instructor-130340-pensacola-main-campus-florida-united-states": {
      "title": "Instructor 130340",
      "description": "Instructor 130340 - Pensacola - Main Campus, Florida, United States My settings Life at UWF About UWF UWF News Pensacola Area Benefits Wellness Program Search Jobs Job Alerts Faculty Jobs Staff Jobs Adjunct Jobs Temporary Jobs Student Jobs Applicant FAQs My Application Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Please review job requirements carefully. Failure to submit all pieces of the application may result in disqualification. Applications are accepted on the University of West Florida career site . For assistance contact UWF Human Resources at 850.474.2694 or jobs@uwf.edu . Instructor 130340 Pensacola - Main Campus, Florida, United States Dept of Social Work Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Usha Kundu, MD College of Health Faculty Full-time Add to favorites View favorites POSITION DETAILS Employment based visa sponsorship will be considered for this position. Position Number: 130340 Classification Title: Instructor Working Title: Instructor in Social Work Department: Dept of Social Work FLSA Status: Exempt Salary Range: Commensurate with experience and education Pay Basis: Annually POSITION OVERVIEW JOB SUMMARY: The Usha Kundu College of Health (UKCOH) Department of Social Work at UWF seeks a dynamic professional to join its cadre of faculty as an Instructor, with a start date of January 4, 2027. This is a 9-month, full-time, non-tenure-track position. The department offers both a Master in Social Work (MSW) that focuses on clinical practice in behavioral and health care settings and a generalist Bachelor in Social Work (BSW) degree, and the selected candidate will be expected to teach across the BSW and MSW curricula, with a primary emphasis on undergraduate courses. Position duties include teaching courses across the social work curriculum (undergraduate and/or graduate courses) and serving as the co-director of the field office, with shared responsibility for overseeing field office processes and data collection to monitor the field office's impact on student learning across the social work curriculum (undergraduate and/or graduate courses). This candidate will also actively engage in curriculum development and department activities. The faculty member is expected to work with municipal and regional service organizations to cultivate field placement sites and provide meaningful service to the department, college, and the profession. Primary responsibilities include the following: • Meet, at a minimum, biweekly with the Department Chair to report on Social Work Field Office activities and concerns. • Consult promptly within 24 hours or at your earliest convenience, taking into account weekends, holidays, and emergency campus closures, with the Chair and /or relevant program coordinator regarding matters related to students, faculty, or staff. • Coordinate strategic planning with the Department Chair, BSW Coordinator, and MSW Coordinator. • Co-Develop and facilitate the Field Office orientation for the UWF SW department. • Co-Develop and maintain the UWF Social Work Field manual. • Maintain compliance with UWF and Department of Social Work policies. • Provide field-related training to seminar instructors, field instructors, and departmental staff. • Provide active supervision of field staff and support personnel. • Manage all aspects of the field education program in collaboration with the BSW Field Director. The University of West Florida, a regional, comprehensive public university serving over 15,000 students, was established in 1963. It is located on a 1,600-acre wooded campus in the westernmost city in the Panhandle region of Florida. Pensacola, the City of Five Flags and the “cradle of naval aviation,” is home to the US Naval Air Station and the Blue Angels (and neighboring Eglin Air Force Base). Pensacola is renowned for its white, sugar-sand beaches and the aquamarine waters of the Gulf of America, labeled the Emerald Coast. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: • Earned a MSW degree from a Council of Social Work Education (CSWE) accredited institution. • Holds an active clinical license in Social Work at the time of appointment. POSITION QUALIFICATIONS: • Earned an MSW degree from a Council of Social Work Education (CSWE) accredited institution. • Holds an active clinical license in Social Work at the time of appointment. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: • Holds a doctoral degree or enrolled in a doctoral program from an accredited institution. • Motivation and demonstrated experience in delivering engaging high-quality online teaching. • Ability to teach foundation courses and advanced clinical courses. • Commitment to purposeful mentoring of BSW and MSW students. Special Requirements or Considerations of the Job: This position requires a criminal background screening. This position requires licensure, certification, or other qualifications described in the Special Instructions. Special Instructions to Applicants: Candidates must apply online through the University of West Florida website: https://careers.uwf.edu. Applicants are required to attach a cv, letter of interest and contact information for three references. References will be contacted upon submission of this application. An opportunity to upload these documents will be provided during the application process. For assistance, please contact Human Resources at 850.474.2694 or email jobs@uwf.edu. If one or more of your advanced degrees is awarded from an institution outside of the United States, UWF will require a credential evaluation and/or translation prior to onboarding. This credential evaluation should include original documents received directly from your institution so that the agency can evaluate and attest that your credential is equivalent to a similar degree earned at a US institution. If your credential is not in English, this evaluation should also include a translation to US English. UWF does not endorse any particular approved agency; however, typically any current National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES) member agency is acceptable. You are advised to check with the agency first to make sure your educational background can be evaluated as some agencies do not evaluate all international degrees. When necessary, these credential evaluations will be requested as part of the Offer Letter with instructions on where and to whom these documents should be submitted. Applicant's must upload a copy of their active clinical license in Social Work with their application. ADDITIONAL POSTING DETAILS Number of Vacancies: 1 Work Hours: 9:00 AM to 5:00 PM, varies based on course assignment FTE: 1.0 Preferred Response Date: 10/5/2026 The University of West Florida is an Equal Opportunity/Access/Disabled/Veteran employer. Any individual requiring special accommodation to apply is requested to advise UWF by contacting UWF Human Resources at 850.474.2694. E-Verify is required for employment. All applications for employment at the University are subject to Florida public records law. Apply First Name (required) b4693b46 Last Name (required) ac1a9b98 Email (required) f3d87fe0 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Apply Now First Name (required) af8428c4 Last Name (required) f567b471 Email (required) 2f618d4e Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you FOLLOW US Accessibility Equal Opportunity About This Site Contact Copyright © 2026 The University of West Florida All Rights Reserved | Disclaimer and Privacy Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. For more information, see UWF's Internet Privacy Statement . Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. If you do not allow these cookie we will not know when you have visited our site, and will not be able to monitor its performance. Manage Cookies I do not accept I accept Save"
