    "https://careers.uwf.edu/jobs/ops-office-support-specialist-pensacola-main-campus-florida-united-states": {
      "title": "OPS Office Support Specialist",
      "description": "OPS Office Support Specialist - Pensacola - Main Campus, Florida, United States My settings Life at UWF About UWF UWF News Pensacola Area Benefits Wellness Program Search Jobs Job Alerts Faculty Jobs Staff Jobs Adjunct Jobs Temporary Jobs Student Jobs Applicant FAQs My Application Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Please review job requirements carefully. Failure to submit all pieces of the application may result in disqualification. Applications are accepted on the University of West Florida career site . For assistance contact UWF Human Resources at 850.474.2694 or jobs@uwf.edu . OPS Office Support Specialist Pensacola - Main Campus, Florida, United States ArgoCard Program Temporary Temporary Add to favorites View favorites POSITION DETAILS Employment based visa sponsorship will NOT be considered for this position. Classification Title: Clerical and Secretarial Working Title: Office Support Specialist Department: ArgoCard Program FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Salary Range: $18.00 Pay Basis: Hourly POSITION OVERVIEW JOB SUMMARY: The Office Support Specialist provides administrative and operational support for the creation, production, and distribution of ID Cards for students, employees, and approved university-affiliated groups. The position serves as one of the primary points of contact for customer service operations, including responding to phone inquiries, email correspondence, and in-person traffic. Responsibilities include verifying documentation, providing information regarding ID card usage and meal plan options, and troubleshooting issues associated with the ID Card Program to ensure compliance with established policies and procedures. This role assists with the collection, reconciliation, and documentation of funds from the Automatic Deposit Machine (ADM), copiers, and change machines in accordance with university cash handling standards. The Office Support Specialist also provides backup support to the BAS IT Senior Coordinator by assisting with basic troubleshooting and coordination related to door access system. This role may also provide back up in resolving issues with student printing, copy services and the point-of-sale (POS) systems and related hardware used by Dining Services. The position helps maintain continuity of operations and ensures timely service delivery across supported systems. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: A high school diploma and two years appropriate experience. Appropriate college coursework or vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. POSITION QUALIFICATIONS: The role requires basic computer proficiency, including the use of email, data entry, and standard office applications. Candidates must be able to handle cash and follow established financial procedures, demonstrate strong organizational skills and attention to detail, communicate effectively both orally and in writing, and handle sensitive or confidential information with discretion. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Candidates with an associate degree or some college coursework in office administration, business, or an IT related field are preferred. Prior experience in a higher education or campus operations environment is also desirable. Familiarity with the Banner Document Management System (BDMS) or similar electronic record systems, as well as experience supporting door access systems or other campus IT/operational systems. Preferred candidates will have experience operating ID card production systems, access control systems, or point of sale (POS) equipment, as well as experience troubleshooting computers, peripheral and software. Knowledge of university policies and procedures, including cash handling and recordkeeping standards. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS/JOB DUTIES: 50% - Produce and issue ID Cards or Badges for students, employees and approved university affiliated groups in accordance with established procedures. Verify identity documentations and ensure accurate data entry within applicable systems. Serve as one of the primary points of contacts in the office by responding to phone calls, emails and in-person inquiries related to ID Card Services and meal plans. Provide information regarding ID Card usage and related services. Troubleshoot and resolve issues associated with the ID Card Program or escalate as appropriate. - (Essential) 30% - Provide backup support to the BAS IT Senior Coordinator by assisting with basic troubleshooting and coordination for door access systems and related equipment. This may include student printing and copy devices, and Dining Services POS systems. Maintain accurate records and documentation for supported systems in accordance with departmental procedures. - (Essential) 10% - Assist the Program Manager with the collection, reconciliation, and documentation of funds from the Automatic Deposit Machine (ADM), copiers, and change machines in accordance with university cash handling procedures. Maintain accurate records to support audit and reporting requirements. - (Essential) 10% - Assist the Program Manager with maintaining student and employee records in accordance with departmental and university policies, including scanning and indexing documents for the Nautilus Card Office within the Banner Document Management System (BDMS). - (Essential) PHYSICAL DEMANDS: Physical Requirements: Occasional and/or light lifting required. Limited exposure to elements such as heat, cold, noise, dust, dirt, chemicals, etc., but none to the point of being disagreeable. May involve minor safety hazards where likely results would be cuts, bruises, etc. Impact of Deadlines: Work schedules, volume of work, or priorities seldom change. Able to anticipate new work. Minimum distractions or interruptions. Seldom involves conflicting demands on time. Standing: Daily Walking: Daily Sitting: Daily Reaching with hands and arms: Daily Climbing or balancing: Occasionally Stooping: Occasionally Use of hands to handle objects: Daily Lifting up to 10lbs: Frequently Lifting up to 25lbs: Occasionally Lifting over 25lbs: Never Talking as express or exchange of ideas verbally: Daily Hearing as perceive sound by ear: Daily Vision as distinguish colors & depth: Daily Special Requirements or Considerations of the Job: This position requires a criminal background screening. This position requires fingerprinting. Special Instructions to Applicants: Candidates must apply online through the University of West Florida website: https://careers.uwf.edu. Applicants are required to attach a resume, cover letter and contact information for three references. An opportunity to upload these documents will be provided during the application process. For assistance, please contact Human Resources at 850.474.2694 or email jobs@uwf.edu. ADDITIONAL POSTING DETAILS Number of Vacancies: 1 Work Hours: 12:00 – 5:00 pm, Monday – Friday, Preferred hours. This part-time position will need to work extended hours during orientation and registration periods and cover staff vacations, as approved. FTE: 0.50 Preferred Response Date: 10/16/2026 The University of West Florida is an Equal Opportunity/Access/Disabled/Veteran employer. Any individual requiring special accommodation to apply is requested to advise UWF by contacting UWF Human Resources at 850.474.2694. E-Verify is required for employment. All applications for employment at the University are subject to Florida public records law. Apply First Name (required) d30058ef Last Name (required) 7cca17d4 Email (required) dc189be0 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Apply Now First Name (required) c2cac9bb Last Name (required) de1a68e5 Email (required) 75abefd2 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you FOLLOW US Accessibility Equal Opportunity About This Site Contact Copyright © 2026 The University of West Florida All Rights Reserved | Disclaimer and Privacy Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. For more information, see UWF's Internet Privacy Statement . Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. If you do not allow these cookie we will not know when you have visited our site, and will not be able to monitor its performance. Manage Cookies I do not accept I accept Save"
