    "https://careers.uwf.edu/jobs/adjunct-instructor-pool-behavior-lab-graduate-level-pensacola-main-campus-florida-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor Pool",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor Pool - Behavior Lab - Graduate Level - Pensacola - Main Campus, Florida, United States My settings Life at UWF About UWF UWF News Pensacola Area Benefits Wellness Program Search Jobs Job Alerts Faculty Jobs Staff Jobs Adjunct Jobs Temporary Jobs Student Jobs Applicant FAQs My Application Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Please review job requirements carefully. Failure to submit all pieces of the application may result in disqualification. Applications are accepted on the University of West Florida career site . For assistance contact UWF Human Resources at 850.474.2694 or jobs@uwf.edu . Adjunct Instructor Pool - Behavior Lab - Graduate Level Pensacola - Main Campus, Florida, United States Continuing Education Adjunct Adjunct Closing on: Jul 27 2027 Add to favorites View favorites POSITION DETAILS Employment based visa sponsorship will NOT be considered for this position. Classification Title: Instructor Working Title: Adjunct Instructor Department: Conferences & Continuing Education FLSA Status: Exempt Salary Range: Commensurate with experience Pay Basis: Annually POSITION OVERVIEW JOB SUMMARY: The Behavior Lab at the University of West Florida is seeking qualified applicants for adjunct teaching positions for graduate level courses in Applied Behavior Analysis. The Behavior Lab maintains a pool of adjuncts for teaching opportunities for upcoming semesters. Applications will be accepted on an on-going basis. Your application will be reviewed by the Behavior Lab. If selected, applicants must provide official transcripts and proof of active certification in good standing. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Holds at least the master's degree in an appropriate specialization or the equivalent qualifications based on professional experience and is otherwise qualified to perform assigned duties. The appointee may engage in teaching, scholarship and creative projects, and/or service and other related activities, but is not eligible for tenure. POSITION QUALIFICATIONS: Applicants must have a master's degree and be a Board Certified Analyst for at least (5) years or have a doctorate degree and be a Board Certified Behavior Analyst for at least (3) years. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Doctorate degree Experience with teaching higher education coursework and supervising potential behavior analysts preferred. Special Requirements or Considerations of the Job: This position requires a criminal background screening. This position requires licensure, certification, or other qualifications described in the Special Instructions. Special Instructions to Applicants: Candidates must apply online through the University of West Florida website: https://careers.uwf.edu. Applicants are required to attach a resume, cover letter and contact information for three references. An opportunity to upload these documents will be provided during the application process. For assistance, please contact Human Resources at 850.474.2694 or email jobs@uwf.edu. The college is building a pool of adjuncts for teaching opportunities for upcoming semesters. Applications will be accepted on an on-going basis. Your application will be reviewed by the appropriate academic department. ADDITIONAL POSTING DETAILS Number of Vacancies: Multiple Work Hours: Dependent on Courses FTE: 0.225 Closing Date: 07/24/2027 The University of West Florida is an Equal Opportunity/Access/Disabled/Veteran employer. Any individual requiring special accommodation to apply is requested to advise UWF by contacting UWF Human Resources at 850.474.2694. E-Verify is required for employment. All applications for employment at the University are subject to Florida public records law. Apply First Name (required) 9bd8c488 Last Name (required) c1ed93c2 Email (required) 6cd1de19 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Apply Now First Name (required) aa483b35 Last Name (required) 87d4f493 Email (required) 879fc027 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you FOLLOW US Accessibility Equ