      "description": "Adjunct Instructor Pool - Behavior Lab - Undergraduate Level - Pensacola - Main Campus, Florida, United States My settings Life at UWF About UWF UWF News Pensacola Area Benefits Wellness Program Search Jobs Job Alerts Faculty Jobs Staff Jobs Adjunct Jobs Temporary Jobs Student Jobs Applicant FAQs My Application Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Please review job requirements carefully. Failure to submit all pieces of the application may result in disqualification. Applications are accepted on the University of West Florida career site . For assistance contact UWF Human Resources at 850.474.2694 or jobs@uwf.edu . Adjunct Instructor Pool - Behavior Lab - Undergraduate Level Pensacola - Main Campus, Florida, United States Continuing Education Adjunct Adjunct Closing on: Jul 23 2027 Add to favorites View favorites POSITION DETAILS Employment based visa sponsorship will NOT be considered for this position. Classification Title: Instructor Working Title: Adjunct Instructor Department: Conferences & Continuing Educ FLSA Status: Exempt Salary Range: Dependent on course and credentials Pay Basis: Annually POSITION OVERVIEW JOB SUMMARY: The Behavior Lab at the University of West Florida is seeking qualified applicants for an adjunct teacher position for undergraduate level courses in Applied Behavior Analysis. The Behavior Lab maintains a pool of adjuncts for teaching opportunities for upcoming semesters. Applications will be accepted on an on-going basis. Your application will be reviewed by the Behavior Lab. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Holds at least the master's degree in an appropriate specialization or the equivalent qualifications based on professional experience and is otherwise qualified to perform assigned duties. The appointee may engage in teaching, scholarship and creative projects, and/or service and other related activities, but is not eligible for tenure. POSITION QUALIFICATIONS: Applicants must have a master's degree or doctorate and be a Board Certified Analyst for at least three (3) years. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Experience with teaching higher education coursework and supervising potential behavior analysts preferred. Special Requirements or Considerations of the Job: This position requires a criminal background screening. Special Instructions to Applicants: Candidates must apply online through the University of West Florida website: https://careers.uwf.edu. Applicants are required to attach a resume, cover letter and contact information for three references. An opportunity to upload these documents will be provided during the application process. For assistance, please contact Human Resources at 850.474.2694 or email jobs@uwf.edu. Board Certified Analyst required. The Behavior Lab maintains a pool of adjuncts for teaching opportunities for upcoming semesters. Applications will be accepted on an on-going basis. Your application will be reviewed by the Behavior Lab. If selected, applicants must provide official transcripts and proof of active certification in good standing. ADDITIONAL POSTING DETAILS Number of Vacancies: Multiple Work Hours: Dependent on Courses FTE: 0.225 Closing Date: 07/23/2027 The University of West Florida is an Equal Opportunity/Access/Disabled/Veteran employer. Any individual requiring special accommodation to apply is requested to advise UWF by contacting UWF Human Resources at 850.474.2694. E-Verify is required for employment. All applications for employment at the University are subject to Florida public records law. Apply First Name (required) fba624fc Last Name (required) 500b6536 Email (required) 013367a4 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Apply Now First Name (required) 8313e2d6 Last Name (required) a8e9ec53 Email (required) 1d5c7ecf Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you FOLLOW US Accessibility Equal Opportunity About This Site Contact Copyright © 2026 The University of West Florida All Rights Reserved | Disclaimer and Privacy Candidate Details This website use