      "title": "Adjunct Instructor Pool",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor Pool - Department of Medical Laboratory Sciences - Pensacola - Main Campus, Florida, United States My settings Life at UWF About UWF UWF News Pensacola Area Benefits Wellness Program Search Jobs Job Alerts Faculty Jobs Staff Jobs Adjunct Jobs Temporary Jobs Student Jobs Applicant FAQs My Application Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Please review job requirements carefully. Failure to submit all pieces of the application may result in disqualification. Applications are accepted on the University of West Florida career site . For assistance contact UWF Human Resources at 850.474.2694 or jobs@uwf.edu . Adjunct Instructor Pool - Department of Medical Laboratory Sciences Pensacola - Main Campus, Florida, United States Medical Laboratory Sciences (MLS) Adjunct Usha Kundu, MD College of Health Adjunct Closing on: Sep 10 2027 Add to favorites View favorites POSITION DETAILS Employment based visa sponsorship will be considered for this position. Classification Title: Instructor Working Title: Adjunct Instructor Department: Medical Laboratory Sciences (MLS) FLSA Status: Exempt Salary Range: Dependent on Course and Credentials Pay Basis: Annually POSITION OVERVIEW JOB SUMMARY: The Department of Medical Laboratory Sciences is seeking qualified part-time adjunct instructors to teach in the following fields: Medical Laboratory Sciences which may include Clinical Chemistry, Hematology, Microbiology, Molecular, Immunology, and Immunohematology or lower-level prerequisite or non-MLS courses such as Clinical Genetics and Clinical Biochemistry or Fundamentals of Microbiology. The college is building a pool of adjuncts for teaching opportunities for upcoming semesters. Applications will be accepted on an on-going basis. Your application will be reviewed by the appropriate academic department. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Holds at least the master's degree in an appropriate specialization or the equivalent qualifications based on professional experience and is otherwise qualified to perform assigned duties. The appointee may engage in teaching, scholarship and creative projects, and/or service and other related activities, but is not eligible for tenure. POSITION QUALIFICATIONS: Master’s degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate field of specialization such as clinical laboratory sciences, biomedical sciences, or biochemistry. Certification as a Medical Laboratory Scientist either as a generalist or in the field that is being taught with the exception of prerequisite courses. Prerequisite and non-MLS core courses do not require an MLS certification. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Master’s or higher degree in an appropriate field of specialization or a closely related discipline from an accredited institution. The ideal candidate will be flexible and creative with experience teaching in both face-to-face and online learning environments, including laboratory courses. Experience in teaching is preferred. Must be certified (unless teaching non-MLS core courses) as an MLS or MT (ASCP preferred) and licensed as an MLS in the state of Florida (preferred) or willing to get a license. Special Requirements or Considerations of the Job: This position requires a criminal background screening. Special Instructions to Applicants: Candidates must apply online through the University of West Florida website: https://careers.uwf.edu. Applicants are required to attach a resume, cover letter and contact information for three references. An opportunity to upload these documents will be provided during the application process. For assistance, please contact Human Resources at 850.474.2694 or email jobs@uwf.edu. The department is building an applicant pool for temporary to permanent part-time or full-time opportunities. Applications will be accepted on an on-going basis. ADDITIONAL POSTING DETAILS Number of Vacancies: Multiple Work Hours: Dependent on Course Schedule FTE: 0.225 Closing Date: 9/10/2027 The University of West Florida 