    "https://careers.uwf.edu/jobs/ops-hsa-department-coordinator-pensacola-main-campus-florida-united-states": {
      "title": "OPS HSA Department Coordinator",
      "description": "OPS HSA Department Coordinator - Pensacola - Main Campus, Florida, United States My settings Life at UWF About UWF UWF News Pensacola Area Benefits Wellness Program Search Jobs Job Alerts Faculty Jobs Staff Jobs Adjunct Jobs Temporary Jobs Student Jobs Applicant FAQs My Application Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Please review job requirements carefully. Failure to submit all pieces of the application may result in disqualification. Applications are accepted on the University of West Florida career site . For assistance contact UWF Human Resources at 850.474.2694 or jobs@uwf.edu . OPS HSA Department Coordinator Pensacola - Main Campus, Florida, United States Health Sciences and Administration Temporary Temporary Add to favorites View favorites POSITION DETAILS Employment based visa sponsorship will NOT be considered for this position. Classification Title: Other Professional (Support/Service) Working Title: OPS HSA Department Coordinator Department: Health Sciences and Administration FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Salary Range: $25.00 per hour Pay Basis: Hourly POSITION OVERVIEW JOB SUMMARY: The Health Sciences and Administration Department Coordinator is responsible for the overall development, implementation, and daily operation of the internship and practicum programs across multiple academic programs in the department including healthcare administration and health sciences. This position also assists with recruitment/marketing for programs in the department, supports faculty with high impact practice implementation, and assists the department with preparations for program reviews and accreditation requirements. This position will teach the internship course. The duties of the position may include, but are not limited to, the following: Internship, Practicum, and Student Placement Coordination - Identify, develop, and maintain internship and practicum opportunities. - Build and maintain relationships with employers and community partners. - Meet with students to support internship preparation, career goals, resumes, and interviewing skills. - Review student portfolios. - Monitor placements and maintain related files, agreements, evaluations, and documentation. - Prepare reports and support data collection for assessment, program review, and accreditation. Outreach and Recruitment - Assist with recruitment and outreach for departmental programs. - Assist with events, information sessions, employer visits, and community presentations. - Promote internship and practicum opportunities to students and external partners. Marketing and Communication - Create marketing materials as needed. - Maintain departmental social media pages. - Support communication with students, employers, alumni, and community partners. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Master’s degree in healthcare administration, health sciences, public health, business administration, or a closely related field from an accredited institution. POSITION QUALIFICATIONS: Experience supporting internship, practicum, capstone, or experiential learning courses in higher education. Experience in healthcare administration, healthcare operations, workforce development, accreditation support, student advising, or employer partnership development. Special Requirements or Considerations of the Job: This position requires a criminal background screening. This position requires fingerprinting. Special Instructions to Applicants: Candidates must apply online through the University of West Florida website: https://careers.uwf.edu. Applicants are required to attach a resume, cover letter and contact information for three references. An opportunity to upload these documents will be provided during the application process. For assistance, please contact Human Resources at 850.474.2694 or email jobs@uwf.edu. ADDITIONAL POSTING DETAILS Number of Vacancies: 1 Work Hours: 8am - 5pm, occasional evenings or weekends may be required with advance notice FTE: 1.0 Preferred Response Date: 7/10/2026 The University of West Florida is an Equal Opportunity/Access/Disabled/Veteran employer. Any individual requiring special accommodation to apply is requested to advise UWF by contacting UWF Human Resources at 850.474.2694. E-Verify is required for employment. All applications for employment at the University are subject to Florida public records law. Apply First Name (required) 17a28d87 Last Name (required) 3c4c2f9e Email (required) 5286b559 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Apply Now First Name (required) 1d8b29f7 Last Name (required) b6ba6209 Email (required) db18138e Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you FOLLOW US Accessibility Equal Opportunity About This Site Contact Copyright © 2026 The University of West Florida All Rights Reserved | Disclaimer and Privacy Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. For more information, see UWF's Internet Privacy Statement . Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. If you do not allow these cookie we will not know when yo