p, and creative projects, and/or service and other related activities, but is not eligible for tenure. POSITION QUALIFICATIONS: Applicants must have a master's degree in education from an accredited institution to teach undergraduate courses, and a doctorate degree in education from an accredited institution to teach graduate courses. Special Requirements or Considerations of the Job: This position requires a criminal background screen. Special Instructions to Applicants: Candidates must apply online through the University of West Florida website: https://careers.uwf.edu . Applicants are required to attach a resume, cover letter, and contact information for three references. An opportunity to upload these documents will be provided during the application process. For assistance, please contact Human Resources at 850.474.2694 or email jobs@uwf.edu. The college is building a pool of adjuncts for teaching opportunities for upcoming semesters. Applications will be accepted on an ongoing basis. Your application will be reviewed by the appropriate academic department. ADDITIONAL POSTING DETAILS Number of Vacancies: Multiple Work Hours: Dependent on course assignment FTE: Varies Closing Date: 6/11/2027 The University of West Florida is an Equal Opportunity/Access/Disabled/Veteran employer. Any individual requiring special accommodation to apply is requested to advise UWF by contacting UWF Human Resources at 850.474.2694. E-Verify is required for employment. All applications for employment at the University are subject to Florida public records law. Apply First Name (required) 9f303b2a Last Name (required) bdb31c1c Email (required) 07e5f958 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Apply Now First Name (required) 7b9586af Last Name (required) f38a5b87 Email (required) 13c91289 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you FOLLOW US Accessibility Equal Opportunity About This Site Contact Copyright © 2026 The University of West Florida All Rights Reserved | Disclaimer and P