      "description": "Adjunct Instructor Pool - Pre-licensure Nursing - Pensacola - Main Campus, Florida, United States My settings Life at UWF About UWF UWF News Pensacola Area Benefits Wellness Program Search Jobs Job Alerts Faculty Jobs Staff Jobs Adjunct Jobs Temporary Jobs Student Jobs Applicant FAQs My Application Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Please review job requirements carefully. Failure to submit all pieces of the application may result in disqualification. Applications are accepted on the University of West Florida career site . For assistance contact UWF Human Resources at 850.474.2694 or jobs@uwf.edu . Adjunct Instructor Pool - Pre-licensure Nursing Pensacola - Main Campus, Florida, United States Nursing Adjunct Adjunct Closing on: Mar 15 2027 Add to favorites View favorites POSITION DETAILS Employment based visa sponsorship will NOT be considered for this position. Classification Title: Instructor Working Title: Adjunct Instructor Department: Nursing FLSA Status: Exempt Salary Range: Dependent on Course and Credentials Pay Basis: Annually POSITION OVERVIEW JOB SUMMARY: The college is building a pool of adjuncts for onsite teaching opportunities for upcoming semesters. Applications will be accepted on an on-going basis. Your application will be reviewed by the appropriate academic department. Clinical instruction for pre-licensure nursing students in acute care (medical-surgical), community health, pediatrics, and/or mental health settings. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Holds at least the master's degree in an appropriate specialization or the equivalent qualifications based on professional experience and is otherwise qualified to perform assigned duties. The appointee may engage in teaching, scholarship and creative projects, and/or service and other related activities, but is not eligible for tenure. POSITION QUALIFICATIONS: A Master's Degree in nursing from an accredited institution, or a bachelor's degree in nursing and a master's degree in a closely related field. A clear unencumbered Florida RN License, compact RN license preferred. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Experience teaching pre-licensure students in the clinical setting. Special Requirements or Considerations of the Job: This position requires a criminal background screening. This position requires licensure, certification, or other qualifications described in the Special Instructions. Special Instructions to Applicants: Candidates must apply online through the University of West Florida website: https://careers.uwf.edu. Applicants are required to attach a resume, cover letter and contact information for three references. An opportunity to upload these documents will be provided during the application process. For assistance, please contact Human Resources at 850.474.2694 or email jobs@uwf.edu. The college is building a pool of adjuncts for teaching opportunities for upcoming semesters. Applications will be accepted on an on-going basis. Your application will be reviewed by the appropriate academic department. ADDITIONAL POSTING DETAILS Number of Vacancies: 10 Work Hours: Varies Contract Period: Dependent upon course availability FTE: 0.225 Closing Date: 3/15/2027 The University of West Florida is an Equal Opportunity/Access/Disabled/Veteran employer. Any individual requiring special accommodation to apply is requested to advise UWF by contacting UWF Human Resources at 850.474.2694. E-Verify is required for employment. All applications for employment at the University are subject to Florida public records law. Apply First Name (required) bdc1fef5 Last Name (required) 3c3532b9 Email (required) 11eafef3 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Apply Now First Name (required) 67e681eb Last Name (required) 9400ea09 Email (required) abee353c Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you FOLLOW US Accessibility Equal Opportunity About This Site Contact Copyright © 2026 The University of West Florida All Rights Reserved | Disclaimer and Privacy Candidate Details This