st have current certification as a nurse practitioner, and licensure as nurse practitioner in the state of Florida. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Experience teaching MSN students in the online setting. If Nurse Practitioner, also required to have current certification and licensure as nurse practitioner in the state of Florida. Special Requirements or Considerations of the Job: This position requires a criminal background screen. This position requires licensure, certification, or other qualifications described in the Special Instructions. Special Instructions to Applicants: Candidates must apply online through the University of West Florida website: https://careers.uwf.edu. Applicants are required to attach a resume, cover letter and contact information for three references. An opportunity to upload these documents will be provided during the application process. For assistance, please contact Human Resources at 850.474.2694 or email jobs@uwf.edu. The college is building a pool of adjuncts for teaching opportunities for upcoming semesters. Applications will be accepted on an on-going basis. Your application will be reviewed by the appropriate academic department. ADDITIONAL POSTING DETAILS Number of Vacancies: 10 Work Hours: Varies Contract Period: Dependent upon course availability FTE: 0.225 Closing: 3/15/2027 The University of West Florida is an Equal Opportunity/Access/Disabled/Veteran employer. Any individual requiring special accommodation to apply is requested to advise UWF by contacting UWF Human Resources at 850.474.2694. E-Verify is required for employment. All applications for employment at the University are subject to Florida public records law. Apply First Name (required) fe485916 Last Name (required) f9d919e4 Email (required) a1ebfc26 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Apply Now First Name (required) 458336b1 Last Name (required) c95ed073 Email (required) 273317c8 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you FOLLOW US Accessibility Equal Opport