    "https://careers.uwf.edu/jobs/adjunct-instructor-pool-respiratory-therapy-pensacola-main-campus-florida-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor Pool",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor Pool - Respiratory Therapy - Pensacola - Main Campus, Florida, United States My settings Life at UWF About UWF UWF News Pensacola Area Benefits Wellness Program Search Jobs Job Alerts Faculty Jobs Staff Jobs Adjunct Jobs Temporary Jobs Student Jobs Applicant FAQs My Application Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Please review job requirements carefully. Failure to submit all pieces of the application may result in disqualification. Applications are accepted on the University of West Florida career site . For assistance contact UWF Human Resources at 850.474.2694 or jobs@uwf.edu . Adjunct Instructor Pool - Respiratory Therapy Pensacola - Main Campus, Florida, United States Health Sciences and Administration Adjunct Adjunct Closing on: Dec 8 2026 Add to favorites View favorites POSITION DETAILS Employment based visa sponsorship will NOT be considered for this position. Position Number: Adjunct Instructor Pool - Respiratory Therapy Classification Title: Instructor Working Title: Adjunct Instructor Department: Health Sciences and Administration FLSA Status: Exempt Salary Range: Dependent on Course and Credentials Pay Basis: Annually POSITION OVERVIEW JOB SUMMARY: Part-time adjunct instructors in the Bachelor of Science in Respiratory Therapy (BSRT) program within the Department of Health Sciences and Administration deliver high-quality instruction across didactic, laboratory, and/or clinical courses. Key responsibilities include providing evidence-based teaching, evaluating student performance, fostering a supportive learning environment, and ensuring alignment with course outcomes and accreditation standards. Adjunct instructors work collaboratively with full-time faculty and participate in required training and course meetings to promote student success and maintain overall program quality. The Bachelor of Science in Respiratory Therapy (BSRT) program is accredited by the Commission on Accreditation for Respiratory Care (CoARC). MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Candidates must meet the following minimum qualifications to be considered: - Earned a Master’s degree in Respiratory Care or closely related discipline from a CoARC-accredited respiratory therapy program. - Valid NBRC Registered Respiratory Therapist (RRT) credential. - Active Respiratory Care License in the state of Florida in good standing. - Relevant respiratory therapy experience, including clinical, academic, and/or managerial roles. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Preferred candidates will hold a doctorate degree in an appropriate field of specialization or a closely related discipline from an accredited institution, beyond the required respiratory care degree. Prior teaching experience in respiratory therapy or related health sciences in online or hybrid teaching formats. 1 year or more experience in areas such as mechanical ventilation, critical care, neonatal/pediatric care, or cardiopulmonary diagnostics; and familiarity with CoARC standards and competency-based education. Advanced credentials Adult Critical Care Specialty (ACCS), Neonatal/Pediatric Specialty (NPS), or Sleep Disorders Specialty CRT-SDS/RRT-SDS) and active involvement in professional organizations such as the American Association for Respiratory Care (AARC) , Florida Society Respiratory Care (FSRC), or related specialty societies. Special Requirements or Considerations of the Job: This position requires a criminal background screen. This position requires licensure, certification, or other qualifications described in the Special Instructions. Special Instructions to Applicants: All applicants will need to upload their current CV and copies of their NBRC Registered Respiratory Therapist (RRT) credential and Florida Respiratory Care License. Candidates must apply online through the University of West Florida website: https://careers.uwf.edu. Applicants are required to attach a CV, letter of interest and contact information for two professional references. References will be contacted upon submission of this application. An opportunity to upload these documents will be provided during the application process. For assistance, please contact Human Resources at 850-474-2694 or email jobs@uwf.edu. The college is building a pool of adjuncts for teaching opportunities for upcoming semesters. Applications will be accepted on an on-going basis. Your application will be reviewed by the Department of Health Sciences and Administration. ADDITIONAL POSTING DETAILS Number of Vacancies: Multiple Work Hours: Dependent on course scheduling FTE: 0.225 Closing Date: 12/8/2026 The University of West Florida is an Equal Opportunity/Access/Disabled/Veteran employer. Any individual requiring special accommodation to apply is requested to advise UWF by contacting UWF Human Resources at 850.474.2694. E-Verify is required for employment. All applications for employment at the University are subject to Florida public records law. Apply First Name (required) 40055817 Last Name (required) dba02bb6 Email (required) 73939cc9 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Apply Now First Name (required) 6caaddec Last Name (required) f8f4cffe Email (required) a38bbd91 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you FOLLOW US Accessibility Equal Opportunity About This Site Contact Copyright © 2026 The University of West Florida All Rights Reserved | Disclaimer and Privacy Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. For more information, see UWF's Internet Privacy Statement . Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. The