    "https://careers.uwf.edu/jobs/associate-director-106300-pensacola-main-campus-florida-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate Director 106300",
      "description": "Associate Director 106300 - Pensacola - Main Campus, Florida, United States My settings Life at UWF About UWF UWF News Pensacola Area Benefits Wellness Program Search Jobs Job Alerts Faculty Jobs Staff Jobs Adjunct Jobs Temporary Jobs Student Jobs Applicant FAQs My Application Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Please review job requirements carefully. Failure to submit all pieces of the application may result in disqualification. Applications are accepted on the University of West Florida career site . For assistance contact UWF Human Resources at 850.474.2694 or jobs@uwf.edu . Associate Director 106300 Pensacola - Main Campus, Florida, United States WUWF - Mgmt & General Administrator Staff Full-time POSITION DETAILS Employment based visa sponsorship will NOT be considered for this position. Position Number: 106300 Classification Title: Associate Director Working Title: Associate Director, Content and Audience Department: WUWF - Mgmt & General FLSA Status: Exempt Salary Range: $70,913 - $77,359 Pay Basis: Annually POSITION OVERVIEW JOB SUMMARY: The Associate Director, Content & Audience is WUWF's program director and chief editor. Starting from the audience (who the station serves, who it is not yet reaching, and what they need), the position leads what WUWF puts on the air and online: the program schedule, news and music, national and local, and the journalism and original content the station creates. The position sets programming and coverage priorities with the team, edits the work, coaches and develops hosts, reporters and producers, builds new programming, and is accountable for audience reach and growth. The position serves on the leadership team, informing station-wide strategy with the other unit leads, and manages the content and programming budget. It is accountable for the station’s editorial integrity and independence, and works with Revenue & Development on sponsorship and member benefits within that standard. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Master’s degree in an appropriate area of specialization and four years of appropriate experience; or a bachelor’s degree in an appropriate area of specialization and six years of appropriate experience. POSITION QUALIFICATIONS: Three years of direct people management, including hiring, coaching and performance conversations. A collaborative leadership style, with a record of building shared plans with staff and peers while holding clear accountability for results. Demonstrated use of audience data, including ratings, streaming and digital analytics, to make programming and editorial decisions, and experience growing audience beyond broadcast. Demonstrated editing across forms, from structural through line level. Working knowledge of journalism ethics, noncommercial media standards, and the FCC requirements that bear on content and programming. Sound judgment under deadline and under public pressure. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: In order of priority: public media leadership experience, and familiarity with NPR standards and the member-station system; experience as a program director, including schedule strategy, audience research, national program acquisition and music programming. Also valued: podcast or original-series development from concept through launch; supervising student or early-career journalists to publication standard and working with university faculty; experience with multi-newsroom collaborations or AI tools in a newsroom setting. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS/JOB DUTIES: 25% - Programming and the broadcast schedule. Serve as program director, accountable for the schedule on 88.1 FM, the HD channels and the streams, including news, music, national and local programming. Use Nielsen, streaming and digital data and listener feedback to adjust the schedule. Lead local music programming with its hosts. Lead national program acquisition and renewals and relationships with NPR and other providers. Communicate schedule decisions to Operations & Technology and Revenue & Development. Coordinate on-air drives with Revenue & Development, scheduling on-air talent and programming around them. Direct on-air sound with on-air staff, and coordinate with Revenue & Development so promos and fundraising and sponsorship spots are recorded by on-air talent and scheduled. Monitor the quality of on-air content, and prepare the quarterly issues and programs list. - (Essential) 20% - Audience growth and platform strategy. Grow WUWF's audience, with accountability for reach and audience succession. Define the audiences WUWF intends to reach before choosing the programs and products meant to reach them. Lead the cycle that produces WUWF's public service priorities through structured community listening. Set and review audience indicators across broadcast and digital and share them with the team to guide programming and editorial decisions. Integrate broadcast, web, newsletter, podcast and social into one content plan with audience staff. Set priorities for promoting WUWF programs and content across broadcast and digital. Lead the response to listener comments, requests and complaints. - (Essential) 35% - Editorial direction, original content and standards. With the newsroom, translate WUWF's public service priorities into recurring coverage themes across platforms. Serve as the editorial leader for the whole organization: set daily and weekly coverage priorities, make assignments, and answer for what WUWF covers and declines to cover. Review the beat structure against community information needs. Edit features, enterprise and explanatory work from structure through line. Lead development of original podcasts, limited-run series and public-affairs formats through a process open to ideas from across the staff. Steward the WUWF Code of Editorial Integrity, set standards for new tools including AI, and support the FCC obligations that originate in the programming and coverage record. Develop editorial collaborations with NPR, statewide public media and regional newsrooms, and pitch WUWF work into national distribution. - (Essential) 20% - People, applied learning and department management. Coach and supervise reporters, hosts, producers and freelance contributors. Keep a regular aircheck cadence with on-air staff and set documented development goals with each team member. Build a two-way feedback culture, lead the team through change, and recruit, hire, develop and retain staff. Lead applied learning as a standing function, with student pathways that recur across semesters, and be accountable for the quality and educational value of student work WUWF publishes and airs. Manage the content and programming budget, and serve as a leadership partner to the Executive Director and the other unit leads. - (Essential) PHYSICAL DEMANDS: Physical Requirements: Occasional and/or light lifting required. Limited exposure to elements such as heat, cold, noise, dust, dirt, chemicals, etc., but none to the point of being disagreeable. May involve minor safety hazards where likely results would be cuts, bruises, etc. Impact of Deadlines: Externally imposed deadlines set and revised beyond one’s control. Interruptions influence priorities. Difficult to anticipate nature or volume of work with certainty beyond a few days. Standing: Daily Walking: Daily Sitting: Daily Reaching with hands and arms: Daily Climbing or balancing: Occasionally Stooping: Occasionally Use of hands to handle objects: Daily Lifting up to 10lbs: Occasionally Lifting up to 25lbs: Occasionally Lifting over 25lbs: Occasionally Talking as express or exchange of ideas verbally: Daily Hearing as perceive sound by ear: Daily Vision as distinguish colors & depth: Daily Special Requirements or Considerations of the Job: This position requires a criminal background screening. This position requires fingerprinting. Special Instructions to Applicants: Candidates must apply online through the University of West Florida website: https://careers.uwf.edu. Applicants are required to attach a resume, cover letter and contact information for three references. An opportunity to upload these documents will be provided during the application process. For assistance, please contact Human Resources at 850.474.2694 or email jobs@uwf.edu. ADDITIONAL POSTING DETAILS Number of Vacancies: 1 Work Hours: 8:00 am - 5:00 pm FTE: 1.0 Preferred Response Date: 11/13/2026 The University of West Florida is an Equal Opportunity/Access/Disabled/Veteran employer. Any individual requiring special accommodation to apply is requested to advise UWF by contacting UWF Human Resources at 850.474.2694. E-Verify is required for employment. All applications for employment at the University are subject to Florida public records law. Apply First Name (required) 802a625f Last Name (required) 3536d9d0 Email (required) a2ae264a Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Apply Now First Name (required) 02dc3a4e Last Name (required) 3a05ac9f Email (required) 93a612ae Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you FOLLOW US Accessibility Equal Opportunity About This Site Contact Copyright © 2026 The University of West Florida All Rights Reserved | Disclaimer and Privacy Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. For more information, see UWF's Internet Privacy Statement . Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. If you do not allow these cookie we will not know when you have visited our site, and will not be able to monitor its performance. Manage Cookies I do not accept I accept Save"
