    "https://careers.uwf.edu/jobs/coordinator-ii-117550-pensacola-main-campus-florida-united-states": {
      "title": "Coordinator II 117550",
      "description": "Coordinator II 117550 - Pensacola - Main Campus, Florida, United States My settings Life at UWF About UWF UWF News Pensacola Area Benefits Wellness Program Search Jobs Job Alerts Faculty Jobs Staff Jobs Adjunct Jobs Temporary Jobs Student Jobs Applicant FAQs My Application Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Please review job requirements carefully. Failure to submit all pieces of the application may result in disqualification. Applications are accepted on the University of West Florida career site . For assistance contact UWF Human Resources at 850.474.2694 or jobs@uwf.edu . Coordinator II 117550 Pensacola - Main Campus, Florida, United States Student Engagement Professional Staff Full-time Closing on: Oct 30 2026 POSITION DETAILS Employment based visa sponsorship will NOT be considered for this position. Position Number: 117550 Classification Title: Coordinator II Working Title: Student Organizations and Events Coordinator Department: Student Engagement FLSA Status: Exempt Salary Range: $52,551 Pay Basis: Annually POSITION OVERVIEW JOB SUMMARY: The Student Organizations and Events Coordinator contributes to programs specific to the student organization population at the University. This position oversees all registration of student organizations and works to support registered student organization officers and advisors. Supports registered student organization spending of annual A&S budget allocations. Responsible for training and advising the Student Organization Council (SOC), the student governing board that actively reviews and approves new registered student organization requests. Works collaboratively with departmental and University partners to promote student engagement on campus through in-person involvement fairs, community service activities, leadership development workshops, and other events. Recommends decisions regarding student involvement events, activities, and programs. Oversees the administration of Argo Pulse platform. Supervises student staff. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Masters degree in an appropriate area of specialization; or a bachelors degree in an appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience. POSITION QUALIFICATIONS: Knowledge of event planning principles. Basic assessment practices and principles for student programs and services. Skill in conflict resolution. Ability to function effectively under pressure and in unexpected or emergency situations. Skill in dealing with multiple constituents and external partners. Ability to troubleshoot problems, and resolve multiple problems simultaneously, and handle sensitive and confidential information. Computing skills, excellent verbal and written communication skills. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Knowledge of student organizations, developing support programs, essential student leadership and/or student development theories and principles. Demonstrate evidence of maturity, good judgment, and creativity; possess effective verbal and written communication skills and a professional demeanor, with ability to make complex decisions; skills in developing, organizing, and leading programs and group training sessions. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS/JOB DUTIES: 30% - Support student organization registration. Work with departmental personnel to finalize registration processes each year and execute those processes. Support Registered Student Organization officers and advisors by way of digital resources and in-person workshops and meetings. Regularly communicate with the student organization community and its leaders regarding institutional policies, regulations, and procedures. Oversight of the Registered Student Organizations spending of A&S annual budget allocations. - (Essential) 20% - Develop and implement a student organization council that reviews and approves new Registered Student Organizations on campus. Advise and provide consistent education and training to the governing board on student organization registration process, expectations, Constitution reviews, and other requirements associated with new student organization registration. Support events coordinated in conjunction with the student governing board. - (Essential) 15% - Collaborate and promote signature programs that enhance student involvement including student organization fairs, student organization recognition opportunities, etc. and recommends decisions regarding these events, activities, and programs. Responsible for coordinating the annual Student Involvement Awards, recognizing outstanding and exemplary student organization performance. Actively engage student organization community with aspects of campus life including Homecoming activities, student tailgates, campus events, and more. Supervise student staff. - (Essential) 15% - Provide regular leadership development workshops that focus on group dynamics, team building, servant leadership, strengths, and other relevant topics for student leaders across campus including SGA, RSOs, FSL, first-year students, and more. Oversee community service programming connecting students to meaningful volunteer opportunities through events such as MLK Day of Service. Will support student organizations in their development of community service initiatives that benefit the local Pensacola community. - (Essential) 10% - Oversee administration of the Argo Pulse student organization management platform; collaborate with external partners regarding use and implementation; educate students, student organizations, and campus departments on Argo Pulse usage and functionality. - (Essential) 5% - Serve on University committees, task forces, and teams as assigned. Represents Student Engagement, the Division of Student Affairs, and/or the University at/on local, state, regional, and/or national events/committees. - (Essential) 5% - Other duties as assigned. - (Essential) PHYSICAL DEMANDS: Physical Requirements: Occasional and/or light lifting required. Limited exposure to elements such as heat, cold, noise, dust, dirt, chemicals, etc., but none to the point of being disagreeable. May involve minor safety hazards where likely results would be cuts, bruises, etc. Impact of Deadlines: Routine deadlines. Usually sufficient lead time. Variance in work volume, seasonal, and predictable. Priorities can be anticipated. Some interruptions are present. Involves occasional exposure to demands/pressures from persons other than immediate sup. Standing: Daily Walking: Daily Sitting: Daily Reaching with hands and arms: Daily Climbing or balancing: Occasionally Stooping: Occasionally Use of hands to handle objects: Frequently Lifting up to 10lbs: Frequently Lifting up to 25lbs: Occasionally Lifting over 25lbs: Occasionally Talking as express or exchange of ideas verbally: Daily Hearing as perceive sound by ear: Daily Vision as distinguish colors & depth: Daily Special Requirements or Considerations of the Job: This position requires a valid driver's license. This position requires a criminal background screening. This position requires fingerprinting. Special Instructions to Applicants: Candidates must apply online through the University of West Florida website: https://careers.uwf.edu . Applicants are required to attach a resume, cover letter and contact information for three references. An opportunity to upload these documents will be provided during the application process. For assistance, please contact Human Resources at 850.474.2694 or email jobs@uwf.edu . ADDITIONAL POSTING DETAILS Number of Vacancies: 1 Work Hours: 8am - 5pm; Monday - Friday; nights and weekends as needed FTE: 1.o Closing Date: 10/30/2026 The University of West Florida is an Equal Opportunity/Access/Disabled/Veteran employer. Any individual requiring special accommodation to apply is requested to advise UWF by contacting UWF Human Resources at 850.474.2694. E-Verify is required for employment. All applications for employment at the University are subject to Florida public records law. Apply First Name (